  "repairs": [
    " Ordered DROP now completes and publishes each persistent table/view before moving to the next target, defers missing names, and preserves earlier completion after later errors. Shared embedded/cluster guards preserve views/sequences on DROP TABLE, raise Go 1347 on wrong DROP VIEW objects, protect classic system tables and reject cached-table DROP at its turn. The incorrect atomic multi-target planner and duplicated missing-name loops are removed. View parsing now accepts explicit LOCAL/CASCADED CHECK OPTION and rejects the stale bare-form success expectation, following Go parser.y. Complete durable job, delete-range, recovery, NextGen reserved-object and remaining mode/materialized-view admission obligations remain unresolved.",
    " Cluster DROP now checks references across the entire original persistent target list before any mutation. It uses the latest persistent catalog so a local temporary child cannot hide a referencing FK, and honors the live foreign_key_checks switch. This is SQL preflight, not the durable owner recheck or distributed FK lifecycle.",
    " CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW now carries the old table ID through schema publication, retiring the replaced catalog entry. Multi-target DROP now publishes one schema difference per completed object through the existing shared DDL authority. Both originating and peer sessions remove every dropped view, including completion before a later error. Complete versioned/lazy schema lifecycle remains unaccepted.",
    " Ordered DROP target completion remains inside one routed SQL observation. Live failed mixed DROP retains all original local/persistent/missing targets, one execution and one error in statements_summary. Internal target publication does not emit replacement SQL observations. Complete planner/runtime metadata remains unresolved."
  ],
  "removals": [
    "Atomic multi-target DROP metadata planner",
    "Duplicated embedded table/view missing-name loops",
    "False parser CHECK OPTION prohibition",
    "Stale bare WITH CHECK OPTION success expectation; replaced with Go 1064 rejection",
    "Two DDL tests of private debug text; replaced with actual SQL code/message checks"
  ],
